//! Every phrasing the search has already been shown, embedded (v2.1 §16.4, V-F08).
//!
//! **Generated. Do not edit by hand.** The source is `fixtures/assistance/find/canonical/` plus
//! every retired held-out corpus; `find_recall.rs` regenerates this file and fails if it
//! differs, so the two cannot drift. Run the tests with `UPDATE_PHRASES=1` to rewrite it.
//!
//! ## Why the engine carries the corpus
//!
//! A hand-written synonym table only covers the phrasings whoever wrote it thought of. Two
//! rounds of independent measurement put a number on that: an extension worth +19.2 points on
//! the corpus it was built from was worth +2.3 points on the next one
//! (`fixtures/assistance/find/heldout-independent-v1-void/README.md`). Adding more words draws
//! the same curve again.
//!
//! Matching a query against the corpus itself generalises along a different axis: shared
//! content words and shared character runs, with nothing enumerating a synonym. `scoring`
//! reaches `score` and 「按分数」 reaches 「分数」 for free.
//!
//! ## Why the retired corpora are in here
//!
//! Every corpus listed above has already been used to extend the vocabulary; it is training
//! data and nothing is held out by leaving it on the shelf. Five registers of phrasing is a
//! better index than one, and the corpus that is *not* here is the only one that matters:
//! `fixtures/assistance/find/heldout-independent/`.

